From 91cbdec68d886d5965cd23fa2646cc6002a5d205 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:49:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): opt-in worker-first portable placement [daveey]
 (#461)

* refactor(kanban): extract conservative portable-card boundary [daveey]

* feat(kanban): enroll portable cards with durable worker-first fences [daveey]

* docs(kanban): expose opt-in worker pools and frozen acceptance map [daveey]

* fix(kanban): preserve legacy routing and bound worker placement retries [daveey]

* fix(kanban): rotate bounded worker reservation batches durably [daveey]

* fix(kanban): retain extracted pin validation after rebase [daveey]

* fix(kanban): route remote guard-hold sweep through worker-node dispatch refusals [daveey]

main 91585980f6 added sweep_remote_guard_holds calling kanban_db_dispatch._local_refusals,
which worker-first replaces with kanban_worker_node.dispatch_refusals (now including
placement-policy fences). Without this every non-dry-run dispatch tick raised AttributeError
after merging main. Test covers a worker-queued policy card's guard hold swept by the home.
